{
 "id": "283-39",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "One of the key things we do here is prefix our method names with 'b_'.",
  "So, when you're working on your Python code, ensure that you start your method names with that prefix.",
  "It's a small detail but an important one for consistency and readability.",
  "We'll go over more guidelines as we progress, but for now, I want you to focus on getting comfortable with our primary programming language, Python.",
  "Start with the basics, and we'll build from there.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you need anything.",
  "First, I want you to avoid using a linter in your code.",
  "It's important that you pay close attention to your work and catch any errors or inconsistencies yourself.",
  "Additionally, I'd like you to start implementing a new naming convention for your class and method names.",
  "For class names, use CamelCase.",
  "It improves readability and is a standard practice in our industry.",
  "And for method names, always start with 'ud_'.",
  "This is a prefix we use here at AXIOM to easily identify user-defined methods.",
  "Consistency in coding style is crucial, especially when working collaboratively.",
  "These conventions will help ensure your code aligns with our team's standards and makes your contributions more easily integrable into our projects.",
  "They'll serve as a strong foundation for your future work, not just here at AXIOM but in any software engineering role."
 ],
